    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0845" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/876: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-20T10:00:00+01:00">August 20, 1935—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 20—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>501. Department’s 136, August 18, 1 p.m., and my 500, August 19, 1 p.m. I took
                    occasion last night to hand to Suvich a copy of the message which I had given to
                    Mussolini in the morning and emphasized the fact that it would not be given to
                    the press by the Department. Suvich asked me what Mussolini had said and I
                    answered that he had declared “It is now too late” but I did not go into further
                    details. Suvich, after referring briefly to Italy’s complaints against <pb
                        facs="0846" n="744" xml:id="pg744"/> Abyssinia, said that the entire case
                    would be presented to the League and repeated assertions consistently expressed
                    by Foreign Office officials to that [<hi rendition="#italic">the?</hi>] effect
                    that Italy did not wish to leave the League.</p>
                <p>Marriner has repeated to me his 704, August 19, 11 a.m. and 710, August 17 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">19</hi>], 6 p.m. to the Department.<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d625-f1"/> Up to the present there has been no inquiry from press
                    circles here as to any step on the part of the American Government in connection
                    with the Italian-Ethiopian conflict.</p>
                <p>Not repeated elsewhere.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
